<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN Amro's EAB Q4 net income up 41 pct.</title>
<headline>ABN Amro's EAB Q4 net income up 41 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth quarter 1996</p>
<p>(millions of dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net income			     33.87   vs  23.94</p>
<p>    Net interest income		  90.37   vs  77.11</p>
<p>    Provision for loan losses	   8.00   vs  15.00</p>
<p>    Other operating income	     24.57   vs  18.71</p>
<p>    Operating expenses		   69.16   vs  62.71</p>
<p>NOTE - EAB, a full-service commercial bank serving the New York metropolitan area, is a fully-owned U.S unit of Dutch ABN Amro Bank NV.</p>
<p>Twelve Months to December 31</p>
<p>    Net income			    134.58   vs 109.47</p>
<p>    Net interest income		 349.08   vs 303.18</p>
<p>    Provision for loan losses	  27.50   vs  43.50</p>
<p>    Other operating income	     85.22   vs  79.09</p>
<p>    Operating expenses		  258.26   vs 239.12</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
